    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1138">

                <pb facs="1036" n="1024" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg1024"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.60d61/18: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Sterling</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-12-07">December 7,
                        1939</date>.<lb/>[Received December 7—6:52 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>268. Following by telephone for Department from Helsinki.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“409. December 7, noon. Secretary General Finnish Foreign Office has just
                        telephoned me by direction Minister for Foreign Affairs stating that Finnish
                        Minister and Legation personnel Moscow expect to leave Moscow for Berlin via
                            Dunaburg<anchor n="20" xml:id="d1138-f1"/> today. He stated German
                        Ambassador as Dean of Diplomatic Corps had been requested to take <pb
                            facs="1037" n="1025" xml:id="pg1025"/> charge of Finnish interests and
                        had referred matter to his Government but German Ambassador doubted it would
                        authorize such action. He reminded me that Finnish Government had previously
                        asked Swedish Government to take over its interests but Soviet Government
                        had refused.</p>
                    <p>Secretary General now inquires whether American Embassy Moscow could be
                        authorized to take charge of Finnish interests or at least of Finnish
                        Legation building. I said I would refer matter to you immediately.
                        Schoenfeld.”</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sterling</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1138-f1" n="20" xml:id="d1138-f1-content">
